  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Presence &amp; expertise: principled, locally-led action in complex crises - Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norwegian Church Aid head office will throughout the programme period implement five global programmes focusing on protection, climate-resilient water, sanitation and hygiene, emergency and food response, anticipatory and climate action and coordination and advocacy. Technical advisors working at Norwegian Church Aids head office will support capacity-building and implementation of quality programmes in country offices within their sector, while leading pilot projects, testing and developing toolkits, and collaborative research. This programme focus specifically on protection, including global initiatives such as Integrating Therapeutic Interventions into GBV case management, building on and expanding Norwegian Church Aids MHPSS work and integrating work on GBV and SRHR, and Solutions to inclusion addressing some of the complex needs of people with compounding vulnerabilities, including persons with disabilities as well as those facing specific challenges that may be invisible and poorly documented, like incontinence.</narrative>
  </description>
